        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Hi all! I took a look around this forum but couldn't seem to find an answer, so I had to make an account just to get some clarification in advance of me running the SCRPG for the first time tomorrow.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In the Urban Infestation one-shot, referring to Myriad creating minions, his Release the Swarm ability says&nbsp;\"create [Max] minions of size [Min]\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If this is done, I assume the following results would be interpreted thus;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Roll of d4=2, d6=3, d12=4* would create 4 minions of size d4</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Roll of d6=2,&nbsp;d12 = 3, d4=4 would create 4 minions of size d6</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Roll of d12=2, d6=3, d4=4 would create 4 minions of size d12</p>\r\n\r\n<p>OR would the [Max] refer to the smallest dice roll that could give that result, so a low-rolling [Max] with a d12 doesn't neccesarily mean the spawning of super-hardcore minions, and all the results above would give 4 minions of size d4? This lines up with Lieutenants having a \"value\" equal to the maximum size of their dice, double of which is the damage needed to remove them without a save.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Thanks for the advice! I'm not sure it hugely matters as long as it's played consistently, but I am curious what the consensus is.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>*Of course, this dice pool was invented to illustrate the example</p>",
